{
  "id": "COMPOUND:6372 - PROTEIN:5832",
  "verbalization": "Acifluorfen is implicated in the biological activity of HuT78 through multiple indirect pathways, all of which involve the modulation of protein kinases and thioredoxin-related pathways. The first pathway links Acifluorfen to dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases, which are targeted by 6-acetonyldihydrochelerythrine, a compound that ultimately affects HuT78. The second and third pathways demonstrate that Acifluorfen also targets thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is further targeted by phorone and rhetsinine, both of which also act on HuT78. These findings suggest that Acifluorfen exerts its effects on HuT78 through a network of downstream targets, possibly by modulating cellular signaling and redox homeostasis. The consistent involvement of protein kinases and thioredoxin pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Acifluorfen influences cellular processes in HuT78, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
